   "overview": "<p>This fashion and textiles course equips you with industry-standard techniques and practical skills using professional workshops, studio and digital design software. You’ll be taught by experience industry professionals to develop your creative vision through:</p><ul><li><strong>Fashion and costume research</strong> – become competent researching the history of fashion and costume and how to use this to inspire your own designs</li><li><strong>Fashion design and construction</strong>– learn how to design, pattern cut and construct unique garments, from concept to finished product</li><li><strong>Costume design and construction</strong> – Understand and practice the specialist skills required in costume design, construction, embellishment and performance</li><li><strong>Textile design</strong> – from initial ideas to final designs – tell a story through textile designs using a variety of mediums</li><li><strong>Props for theatre &amp; film</strong>– learn prop-making techniques for stage and screen productions</li><li><strong>Digital design</strong>– build a portfolio of styling, branding and visual storytelling using Adobe Creative Cloud</li><li><strong>Sustainability in fashion &amp; costume</strong>– discover how to work as an ethical, environmentally conscious designer</li></ul><p>Through lectures, workshops, industry briefs and live projects, you’ll refine your craft in our specialist sewing, textile and prop-making workshops, photography studios and IT suites.</p><p><strong>Industry Experience &amp; Enrichment</strong></p><p>We believe in hands-on experience, giving you the chance to:</p><ul><li>Work on live industry briefs, designing costumes and props for theatrical productions and fashion editorials</li><li>Exhibit your work in professional showcases</li><li>Collaborate with industry professionals, gaining insight from guest speakers and theatre practitioners, including Chelmsford Theatre</li><li>Create your own professional website and brand identity to launch your career</li></ul><p><strong>We also offer exciting field trips, with past experiences including:</strong></p><ul><li>Theatre shows, backstage and costume department tours</li><li>Harry Potter Studio Tour &amp; cinema screenings</li><li>Visits to The Fashion &amp; Textile Museum and The Victoria &amp; Albert Museum</li><li>Leading London exhibitions and galleries</li></ul>",
