   "qualification": "Level 1 Diploma in Plumbing Studies",
   "courseForMe": "<p>If you are passionate about pursuing a career in plumbing, this exciting qualification is an excellent option for you. This course is suitable for beginners as a first step into the construction industry. The plumbing industry is always in high demand and offers a wide range of opportunities for growth and advancement. During this programme, you will learn basic skills and advance your knowledge whilst being supervised as you undertake various practical and knowledge-based activities.</p>",
   "overview": "<p>This course covers various units to ensure you’re equipped with the necessary skills and knowledge to progress into the career you wish. Units of study you can expect to study:</p><ul><li>Installation, repair, and maintenance of plumbing systems</li><li>Above-ground drainage</li><li>Pipework (copper, plastic, low carbon steel)</li><li>Plumbing science</li></ul><p>Core units will also include:</p><ul><li>Structure of the construction industry</li><li>Fundamental safe working practices</li><li>Environmental and sustainability measures in domestic dwellings</li><li>Site preparation in the construction industry.</li></ul>",
   "employability": "<p>Upon completion of this course, you could progress on to</p><ul><li><p>Level 2 Plumbing full time</p></li></ul><p>Career opportunities may include employment in the construction industry, or you could undertake an apprenticeship in plumbing.</p>",
   "eligibility": "<p>2 GCSEs grades 9-3 in English and Maths</p>",
