   "startIso": "2026-09-01",
   "qualification": "EAL Level 1 Diploma in Engineering Technologies",
   "courseForMe": "<p>This course is designed to offer a comprehensive understanding of the engineering industry to learners who are interested in gaining a fundamental knowledge of the subject. The course material covers a wide range of topics, including the basic principles of engineering and the role of engineers in different industries. It is a great opportunity for individuals who are considering pursuing a career in engineering.</p>",
   "overview": "<p>The course is made up of one externally examined unit, which is mandatory and 8 additional units as follows:</p><ul><li>Introduction to working in engineering (external exam).</li><li>Introduction to machining engineering materials (unit 2).</li><li>Introduction to cutting, forming and assembling engineering materials (unit3).</li><li>Introduction to electronics (unit 5).</li><li>Introduction to electrical installation (unit 6).</li><li>Introduction to cycle maintenance (unit 11).</li><li>Introduction to basic maths and science used in engineering (unit 13).</li><li>Introduction to CAD - computer aided drawing (unit 15).</li><li>Project (unit 17).</li></ul>",
   "employability": "<p>Progression to further study could include the level 2 VRQ Diploma in Engineering Technologies or an apprenticeship such as the level 2 Engineering Operative standard.</p><p>Career opportunities may include operative, trainee or technician positions in the engineering and manufacturing sectors.</p>",
   "eligibility": "<p>2 GCSEs grades 9-2 in English and Maths</p>",
   "assessment": "<ul><li>External exam (online)</li><li>Internal assessments consisting of practical evidence and knowledge tests for each unit. Learners are required to pass each knowledge assessment to complete the unit.</li><li>Practical evidence for each unit from a mixture of made items, printed images, report writing and witness checklists.</li></ul>",
   "fees": "<p>Please contact for details</p>",
   "additionalFees": "<p>Approx. £50:</p><ul><li>Steel toe cap safety boots.</li><li>Overalls or dust coat (blue).</li><li>Scientific calculator.</li><li>Maths set.</li><li>Stationery.</li><li>Padlock for locker.</li></ul>",
