   "qualification": null,
   "courseForMe": "<p>If you are considering a career in the public services sector, this uniformed services course could be the ideal stepping stone for you. Designed specifically for individuals interested in exploring the wide range of opportunities available within public services, this course will give you an in-depth understanding of what it takes to join various uniformed services, such as the police, fire service, ambulance service, and military. Throughout the course, you will engage with a combination of public service and employability units that are structured to help you develop essential transferable skills. These skills are crucial not only for a successful career in public service but also for everyday life. You will learn effective communication, teamwork and problem-solving skills—capabilities that are highly valued across all sectors. Moreover, the curriculum is tailored to provide you with the knowledge and understanding of the key requirements, responsibilities, and challenges faced by professionals in this field. By the end of the course, you will have a clearer vision of your career path and the skills necessary to thrive in a public service role, making a positive impact in your community and beyond.</p>",
   "overview": "<p>This course includes 30 hours of work-related experience and covers various topics to ensure that upon successful completion, you are equipped with the essential skills and knowledge to progress to your next steps.</p><p><strong>Units covered throughout this uniformed services course include:</strong></p><ul><li>Investigate Employment Opportunities in the Uniformed Services</li><li>Wellbeing and Physical Fitness for the Uniformed Services</li><li>Team Working Skills in the Uniformed Services</li><li>Developing Self-Discipline for the Uniformed Services</li><li>Health and Safety in the Uniformed Services</li><li>Carry Out Map Reading and Navigation</li><li>Participate in Competitive Sport</li><li>Participate in an Adventurous Activity</li><li>Explore Volunteering and Volunteering Opportunities</li></ul>",
