   "overview": "<p>The BTEC Level 3 in Information Technology (IT) is a specialist, work-related qualification designed for post-16 learners who are interested in a practical and theoretical approach to IT.</p><p>If you're contemplating studying this IT course, here's some key facts about this course to help you decide:</p><p><strong>What Will You Study?</strong></p><ul><li>The course covers a wide range of IT topics, including:</li><li>Information Technology Systems</li><li>Creating Systems to Manage Information</li><li>Using Social Media in Business</li><li>Programming</li><li>Data Modelling</li><li>Website and Mobile App Development</li><li>Cyber Security and Incident Management</li></ul><p>You will complete both practical assignments and theory-based work, often linked to real-world business scenarios to equip you with the necessary skills and knowledge needed when finding a job within IT.</p>",
   "employability": "<p>The BTEC Level 3 IT is equivalent to up to three A Levels, making it a strong route to university, higher apprenticeships, or direct employment.</p><p>Graduates can pursue careers in:</p><ul><li>Software development</li><li>Web and games design</li><li>IT support and technical roles</li><li>Cyber security</li><li>Business analysis</li></ul><p>The course is also a stepping stone to further study in computing, IT, or related fields at university.</p>",
